        "description": "A 3x3 grid (x left-to-right, y top-to-bottom). LOAD stores the shape shown on `see`. Output img continuously shows the remembered shape 2 steps late. Command CMD0: move the shape one cell down; cells pushed past the border disappear, then rotate the remembered shape 90 degrees clockwise about the grid centre. Command CMD1: rotate the shape 180 degrees. Command CMD2: mirror the shape left-right, then move the shape one cell right, wrapping around the right border. Command CMD3: if the shape has a cell in the top row, then move the shape one cell left; cells pushed past the border disappear; otherwise thicken the shape: every on cell also turns on its 4 neighbours. Decided on the shape just before the command; the result appears as the state 4 steps later; the environment sends no other command in between."
      }
