        "description": "A 3x3 grid (x left-to-right, y top-to-bottom). LOAD stores the shape shown on `see`. Output img continuously shows the remembered shape 2 steps late. Command CMD0: rotate the shape 90 degrees counter-clockwise, then rotate the shape 90 degrees counter-clockwise. Command CMD1: reflect the shape across the main diagonal (x <-> y). Command CMD2: thicken the shape: every on cell also turns on its 4 neighbours, then move the shape one cell left; cells pushed past the border disappear. Command CMD3: rotate the shape 90 degrees counter-clockwise, then reflect the shape across the main diagonal (x <-> y). Query qcell (one cell): output cellon = whether that cell is on, 3 steps after the query, as of just before the query. Output any_all: 1 iff the shape has a cell in anywhere, 3 steps late. Command CMD4: if the shape has a cell in the bottom row, then move the shape one cell left; cells pushed past the border disappear; otherwise move the shape one cell right, wrapping around the right border. Decided on the shape just before the command; the result appears as the state 4 steps later; the environment sends no other command in between."
